      "worked": "From $A+C=A$, $C=0$. Since the values are distinct, $F\\ne0$, so $FD=F$ gives $D=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}B-G&=G\\\\B&=2G\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $B\\le7$ and neither $G=0$ nor $G=1$ is available, $G$ is 2 or 3. Also, $B\\div H=G$ gives $H=2$. Hence $G\\ne2$, because $G$ and $H$ have distinct values. Therefore $G=3$ and $B=6$.\n\nThe remaining values for $A$, $E$ and $F$ are 4, 5 and 7. From $A+H=E$ and $E-G=F$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=A+2\\\\F&=E-3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe only remaining pair differing by 2 is $A=5$, $E=7$. Thus $F=7-3=4$.\n\nTherefore, $A=5$, $B=6$, $C=0$, $D=1$, $E=7$, $F=4$, $G=3$ and $H=2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
